WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.600
Module 1: hardening what stays.

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:07.962
A migration off AD CS takes months, and
for some workloads it never finishes.

3
00:00:07.962 --> 00:00:13.453
Throughout that time the enterprise CA
keeps issuing certificates that domain

4
00:00:13.453 --> 00:00:19.025
controllers, VPN gateways, RADIUS servers
and Entra ID accept as proof of identity.

5
00:00:19.025 --> 00:00:23.942
A CA can create credentials the whole
environment trusts, so one over-privileged

6
00:00:23.942 --> 00:00:28.713
account or misconfigured setting on it
can undo every other identity control.

7
00:00:28.713 --> 00:00:33.550
That makes hardening the first technical
workstream, not a cleanup task at the end.

8
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.219
Everything in this module is defensive:

9
00:00:36.219 --> 00:00:40.490
what each misconfiguration is, how
to detect it, and how to fix it.
